 "unknowns": [
  {
   "configuration_id": "quantum_design_mpms3_lhe_vsm_eto_fosh",
   "key": "vacuum.available",
   "why": "The quote is there, but it only shows how the sample is cooled. It does not say the sample space cannot be evacuated. The same document (p.7, Oven) says the oven option adds 'a turbo pump unit for generating high vacuum in the sample chamber'. So vacuum is an existing option, and the repo convention (PPMS classic, TeslatronPT) would be flag true / optional_not_installed, not false / installed."
  },
  {
   "configuration_id": "quantum_design_mpms3_lhe_vsm_eto_fosh",
   "key": "pressure.base",
   "why": "This absence is inferred from the cooling description. It is not an explicit statement or a complete spec. The oven option evacuates the sample chamber with a turbo pump, so 'no base pressure exists' is wrong. At most it is optional_not_installed with an unknown value."
  },
  {
   "configuration_id": "quantum_design_mpms3_lhe_vsm_eto_fosh",
   "key": "sample.diameter.max",
   "why": "'Sample chamber I.D. 9 mm' is the bore of the temperature-control insert ('9 mm sample bore'), not the largest sample. The repo stores bores as sample.bore_diameter (see the PPMS 25 mm). The holder also takes up space inside the bore, so 9 mm as the largest sample overstates it. It should be re-keyed as sample.bore_diameter = 9 mm."
  }
 ],
